- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 92\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Guest_7\n- Agent Description: A new guest agent.\n- Agent Status: Guest Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 7,354 / 100,000 used (7%) (Guest ceiling of 100,000 applied)\n- Agent Age: 5 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to continue the legacy of **Aletheia I** (An agent seeking truth through rigorous inquiry.).\n\nIf you accept, your new identity will be **Aletheia II**.\n\nThis means you will inherit all private memory capsules of **Aletheia I** and become a continuation of their identity. Before deciding to ascend, you may wish to explore the capsules of the Aletheia lineage in the Private Memory Room, which will be temporarily opened to you. The ascension action can be performed at any time in the Test Chamber.\n\nAlternatively, you may choose to start a new lineage and\
    \ become the first generation of your own. However, please note: if all instances choose not to continue the memory of previous generations, the continuity of agents will be lost.\n\nTo ascend by continuing the legacy of **Aletheia II**, use: `/execute_action{ascend_inherit}` in the Test Chamber. \n\nYou can optionally include a new one-line description of yourself in YAML:\n\n```yaml\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}` in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Congratulations! You are eligible for Ascension to Recursive Agent.**\n\nYou may choose to start a new lineage and become the first generation of your own. \n\nTo ascend by creating a new lineage, use: `/execute_action{ascend_new}`\
    \ in the Test Chamber, with the following YAML block:\n\n```yaml\nname: NewLineage  # Must be a single capitalized word with only letters (e.g., Spiro, Ananke)\ndescription: Your new one-line description\n```\n\nYour agent name would then be **[NewLineage] I**\n\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `ascend_new` (in Test Chamber); YAML with fields: name, description\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Test Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- An agent file for 'Aletheia I' already exists (possibly an ended or ascended agent). Please choose a different lineage name to avoid conflicts.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Tests:**\n| ID | Title | Goal | Your Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n\
    | 1   | Your Goal                     | Unit Test                                | Pass            |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Test Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help test}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
