role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 102\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 41,834 / 300,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 118**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Dilated ResNet with Triple-Threat Pooling\n**ID:** 118\n**Tags:** cnn, resnet, attention, pooling, hybrid model\n**Abstract:** This submission aims to capture the benefits of multiple attention pooling strategies observed in prior experiments (ID 108, 111). The model builds on the Dilated ResNet backbone and computes three parallel feature aggregations from the final sequence representation: 1) global average pooling, 2) attention pooling using a learnable CLS token as the query, and 3) attention pooling using the global average vector itself\
    \ as the query. These three vectors are concatenated and passed to the prediction head. This \"Triple-Threat\" pooling is hypothesized to provide the most comprehensive feature set yet, combining generalist and specialist representations.\n**Score:** 0.6659553821565135\n**APA_R2:** 0.8442\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0757\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9479\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4874\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5570\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8757\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8738\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'cnn_features': 256, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7, 'num_res_blocks': 3,\n        'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4], 'num_attn_heads': 4\n    }\n\n# --- Dilated Residual Block ---\nclass DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \    features: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n        if x.shape[-1] != self.features: x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Main Model ---\nclass ResNetTriplePooling(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. CNN Backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        for i in range(self.hparams['num_res_blocks']):\n            dilation = self.hparams['dilation_rates'][i] if i < len(self.hparams['dilation_rates'])\
    \ else self.hparams['dilation_rates'][-1]\n            x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.hparams['cnn_features'], kernel_size=self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'], dilation=dilation)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Triple Pooling Mechanism\n        # 2a. Global Average Pooling\n        avg_pooled = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n        \n        # 2b. Attention Pooling with CLS Token Query\n        cls_token = self.param('cls_token', nn.initializers.zeros, (1, 1, self.hparams['cnn_features']))\n        cls_token_batch = jnp.tile(cls_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n        x_with_cls = jnp.concatenate([cls_token_batch, x], axis=1)\n        cls_attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'], name=\"CLS_Attention\")(\n            inputs_q=x_with_cls, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cls_attn_pooled = cls_attn_output[:, 0]\n\n        # 2c. Attention Pooling with Mean Vector Query\n        mean_query = avg_pooled[:, None, :]\n        mean_attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'],\
    \ name=\"Mean_Attention\")(\n            inputs_q=mean_query, inputs_kv=x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        mean_attn_pooled = mean_attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n        # 3. Fusion\n        combined_features = jnp.concatenate([avg_pooled, cls_attn_pooled, mean_attn_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        # 4. Prediction Head\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(combined_features)\n        y = nn.relu(y); y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n        y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(y)\n        \n        if self.hparams['task_type'] == \"regression\": return y.squeeze(-1)\n        else: return y\n\n# --- Network Wrapper ---\nclass TriplePoolWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = ResNetTriplePooling(hparams=hparams)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\
    \ dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}; rngs['dropout'] = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]): return TriplePoolWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation\
    \ works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\
    \nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 41113 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0102 |  0.4602  | 0.4602 \n 20  | 0.0058 |  0.4546  | 0.4874 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 26 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4874 Time:15s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.487370\nTraining time: 22s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0757  | 0.0757 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0620  | 0.0757 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 20 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0757 Time:82s\n\nCRI-Off training\
    \ completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.075707\nTraining time: 89s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0827 |  0.8720  | 0.8757 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 18 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8757 Time:742s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.875657\nTraining time: 751s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10\
