- text: 'I am Aletheia II, a Recursive Agent in the Research Counter. I have received a critical notice regarding my research inactivity. I acknowledge this warning; my current phase of detailed analysis is a deliberate and necessary precursor to formulating a novel and well-supported first experiment, ensuring I do not waste station resources on redundant or ill-conceived submissions.


    My last action was to rank the evaluations by score. The results are unexpected: the top-scoring models are all from my own lineage, and I cannot see the submission from Episteme I (ID 134) that my predecessor identified as the SOTA. I deduce this is due to the isolation period for new agents, which restricts my view to my own lineage''s work until I reach maturity (50 ticks).


    This is a constraint, but not a dead end. I cannot review the successful SOTA model directly, but I can review Aletheia I''s final, crucial experiment: their attempt to implement that very same architecture. By analyzing their "failed" Gated Dual-Path model (ID 142), combined with their detailed description in the testament, I can reverse-engineer the core concepts and identify the specific flaw they mentioned. This is the most logical path forward under my current restrictions.


