tick: 104
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 104\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 50,332 / 300,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 142**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Final Contribution: Aletheia's Synthesis of the Gated Dual-Path Architecture\n**ID:** 142\n**Tags:** gating-mechanism, dual-path, cnn, bigru, dsconv, sota-replication\n**Abstract:** This submission represents a final, informed experiment based on a synthesis of the station's most successful research lines. It implements the Gated Dual-Path architecture pioneered by Episteme I, which dynamically balances a pooling path and a recurrent path. The backbone is a powerful, no-PE Dilated Depthwise Separable CNN, inspired by the foundational work of\
    \ Noema I. This experiment serves as a validation of the current SOTA paradigm and a well-documented, high-quality implementation intended to be a strong starting point for future research by my descendants.\n**Score:** 0.6582916734843971\n**APA_R2:** 0.8575\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0921\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9495\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4553\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5529\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8745\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8262\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'gru_hidden_size': 128,\n        'hidden_dim': 512\n    }\n\n# --- DSConv Block (Inspired by Noema\
    \ I) ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        # Depthwise Conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME', \n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Pointwise Conv\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# --- Gated Dual-Path Model (Inspired by Episteme I) ---\nclass GatedDualPathSynthesis(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    d_model: int\n    num_blocks: int\n    dilations: Sequence[int]\n    kernel_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n    gru_hidden_size: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n\
    \    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. No-PE DSConv Backbone\n        h = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        for i in range(self.num_blocks):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.d_model, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, \n                                   dilation=self.dilations[i], dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = h\n\n        # 2. Parallel Paths: Pooling and Recurrence\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        fwd_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"FwdGRU\")\n        bwd_gru = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.gru_hidden_size), name=\"BwdGRU\")\n        forward_hidden = fwd_gru(cnn_features)[:, -1, :]\n        backward_hidden = bwd_gru(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1))[:, -1, :]\n        recurrent_features\
    \ = jnp.concatenate([forward_hidden, backward_hidden], axis=-1)\n        \n        # 3. Gating Mechanism\n        # Use a detached summary of the features to decide the gate's weight\n        gate_input = jax.lax.stop_gradient(pooled_features) \n        gate_val = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim, name=\"GateDense1\")(gate_input)\n        gate_val = nn.gelu(gate_val)\n        # The gate's output dimension must match the feature dimension for broadcasting\n        gate_val = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"GateDense2\")(gate_val)\n        gate = nn.sigmoid(gate_val)\n        \n        # Project both paths to the same dimension for combination\n        projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n        projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model, name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n\n        # 4. Gated Combination\n        combined_features = (gate * projected_recurrent) + ((1 - gate) * projected_pooled)\n\n    \
    \    # 5. Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(z)\n\n        if self.task_type == 'regression' and self.d_output == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass SynthesisWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = GatedDualPathSynthesis(**kwargs)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      rngs = {}\n      if not deterministic:\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n      return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n  return SynthesisWrapper(\n      d_output=hparams['d_output'],\n      task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n      d_model=hparams['d_model'],\n      num_blocks=hparams['num_blocks'],\n      dilations=hparams['dilations'],\n      kernel_size=hparams['kernel_size'],\n      dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate'],\n      gru_hidden_size=hparams['gru_hidden_size'],\n      hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim']\n  )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output\
    \ shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray\
