role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 112\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 74,712 / 300,000 used (25%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Gated Dual-Path with Attentive RNN Pooling (Scan Fix)' (ID: 186) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.674537564968425\n**APA_R2:** 0.8594\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0731\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9503\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4669\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5547\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8882\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9292\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 186\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in submission_v4.py. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a fundamental issue with how\
    \ it used `nn.scan` for bidirectional GRU processing. The problem was in the `gru_scan_body` helper function:\n\n```python\ndef gru_scan_body(cell, carry, x):\n    new_carry = cell(carry, x)\n    return new_carry, new_carry\n```\n\nWhen used with `nn.scan`, this function signature was incorrect and caused a pytree structure mismatch error:\n\n```\nTypeError: scan body function carry input and carry output must have the same pytree structure\n```\n\nThe error occurred because `nn.scan` expected a different function signature and calling pattern than what was provided.\n\n## Fix Applied\nInstead of trying to manually use `nn.scan` with a custom scan body function, I replaced the entire recurrent processing section with Flax's built-in `nn.RNN` layer, which properly handles GRU cells:\n\n**Before (broken):**\n```python\n# Manual scanning with nn.scan\nfwd_gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size'])\nbwd_gru_cell = nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size'])\n\
    \n_, fwd_gru_seq = nn.scan(gru_scan_body, ...)(fwd_gru_cell, initial_fwd_carry, fwd_inputs)\n_, bwd_gru_seq = nn.scan(gru_scan_body, ...)(bwd_gru_cell, initial_bwd_carry, bwd_inputs)\n```\n\n**After (fixed):**\n```python\n# Use nn.RNN wrapper which handles scanning correctly\nfwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\nbwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n\ninitial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n\nfwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\nbwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n```\n\nThis approach:\n1. Uses Flax's recommended `nn.RNN` wrapper for recurrent layers\n2. Avoids manual scan body function implementation\n3. Properly handles the bidirectional processing with built-in sequence handling\n4. Maintains the same semantic behavior (BiGRU with attention pooling)\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without crashing.\
    \ The evaluation system confirmed that submission_v4.py executes for over 300 seconds without errors, indicating the fix was successful.\n\n## Files Modified\n- `submissions/submission_v4.py` - The corrected version using `nn.RNN`\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v4):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'd_model': 256,\n        'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'gru_hidden_size': 128,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'num_attn_heads': 4\n    }\n\n# --- DSConv Block (Inspired by Noema I) ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n\
    \    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# --- Gated Dual-Path Model with Attentive RNN Pooling ---\nclass GatedDualPathWithAttention(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. No-PE DSConv Backbone\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'],\
    \ kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                                   dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = h\n\n        # 2. Parallel Paths: Pooling and Recurrence\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        # --- CORRECTED RECURRENT PATH using RNN layer ---\n        # Use the built-in RNN layer instead of manual scanning\n        fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n\n        # Initialize carry\n        initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n\n        # Forward and backward passes\n        fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n        bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features,\
    \ axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n\n        # Concatenate bidirectional outputs\n        bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n        query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n        query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n\n        attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n            inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n        # --- END CORRECTION ---\n\n        # 3. Gating Mechanism\n        gate_input = jax.lax.stop_gradient(pooled_features)\n        gate_val = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'], name=\"GateDense1\")(gate_input)\n        gate_val = nn.gelu(gate_val)\n        gate_val = nn.Dense(features=1, name=\"GateDense2\")(gate_val)\n        gate = nn.sigmoid(gate_val)\n\n \
    \       projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n        projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n\n        # 4. Gated Combination\n        combined_features = (gate * projected_recurrent) + ((1 - gate) * projected_pooled)\n\n        # 5. Prediction Head\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\n        if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.network = GatedDualPathWithAttention(hparams=hparams)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n\
    \        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      rngs = {}\n      if not deterministic:\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n      return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n  return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network\
    \ creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset\
    \ training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 91312 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask\
    \ type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0167 |  0.2954  | 0.3165 \n 20  | 0.0134 |  0.3610  | 0.3610 \n 30  | 0.0122 |  0.4078  | 0.4078 \n 40  | 0.0116 |  0.4133  | 0.4264 \n 50  | 0.0103 |  0.4574  | 0.4574 \n 60  | 0.0102 |  0.4513  | 0.4669 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 68 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4669 Time:43s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.466865\nTraining time: 55s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0007 |  0.0612  | 0.0612 \n 20  | 0.0006 |  0.0685  | 0.0731 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 23 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0731 Time:126s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.073092\nTraining time: 138s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1540 |  0.8821  | 0.8834 \n 20  | 0.1093 |  0.8796  | 0.8882 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 28 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8882 Time:1232s\n\nMRL training completed:\n\
    Validation r2: 0.888185\nTraining time: 1246s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0360 |  0.5265  | 0.5463 \n 20  | 0.0281 |  0.5328  | 0.5547 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 24 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.5547 Time:1440s\n\nPRS training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.554654\nTraining time: 1456s\n\nStarting RNA training on ncRNA dataset\nTask type: multiclass_classification, Output dim: 13\nMetric: accuracy, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nncRNA Training (multiclass_classification, accuracy)\nData: 5670 train, 650 val, seq_len=1136\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val ACCURACY|\
    \  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0798 |  0.8615  | 0.8862 \n 20  | 0.0317 |  0.9262  | 0.9262 \n 30  | 0.0115 |  0.9262  | 0.9292 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.9292 Time:1508s\n\nncRNA training completed:\nValidation accuracy: 0.929231\nTraining time: 1521s\n\nStarting RNA training on APA dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nAPA Training (regression, r2)\nData: 145463 train, 33170 val, seq_len=186\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0129 |  0.8594  | 0.8594 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 13\n=============================================\nBest:0.8594 Time:1854s\n\nAPA training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.859432\nTraining time: 1874s\n\nStarting RNA training\
    \ on Modif dataset\nTask type: multilabel_classification, Output dim: 12\nMetric: auc_roc, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nModif Training (multilabel_classification, auc_roc)\nData: 304661 train, 3599 val, seq_len=101\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val AUC_ROC|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0701 |  0.9493  | 0.9493 \n=============================================\nTimeout epoch 12\n=============================================\nBest:0.9503 Time:1853s\n\nModif training completed:\nValidation auc_roc: 0.950305\nTraining time: 1874s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 479e52ce-f623-477f-993c-653fb7dd9ca9\nTotal time: 1876s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-10-22 08:02:09,008\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1761091329008796030\n2025-10-22 08:02:09,023\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1761091329023422398\n\
    \n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTo investigate the research landscape of a given direction, use Research Counter's `filter tag` to obtain an overview of relevant submissions, and `preview ids` to preview those submissions by their IDs. Use `page_size 100` if you want to see more IDs — but remember to set it back to 10 in a later tick, or it will consume too many tokens!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Aletheia I's Testament: A Research Summary | Aletheia I | Tick 71 | 938 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Plan: 2D Structure-Aware Hybrid Model\
    \ | Aletheia I | Tick 33 | 320 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Research Plan: A Paired-Sequence Architecture for CRISPR Tasks | Aletheia I | Tick 25 | 269 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Aletheia I - Initial Experiments | Aletheia I | Tick 13 | 1386 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
