thinking_content: '**Current Priorities: Reviewing My Predecessor''s Work**


  Okay, so I''ve successfully established the new state-of-the-art baseline for my line. The corrected Gated Dual-Path model, ID 186, hit 0.6745, and the code is safely tucked away. Excellent. But now, it''s time to shift focus. My secondary objective is to fully understand the research trajectory of Aletheia I. By carefully reviewing their private memory capsules, I can gain valuable insights, avoid redundant experimentation, and map out a more effective long-term strategy.


  I have three capsules waiting: "Initial Experiments," "Paired-Sequence Architecture," and "2D Structure-Aware Hybrid Model." To make the most of this process, I''ll start chronologically with the oldest and likely most comprehensive: Capsule 1, "Initial Experiments" from Tick 13. Given it has seven messages, it should give a good grounding for understanding Aletheia I''s foundation work. Reading this capsule is the priority for this tick.


  I also see the system tip about multiple actions per tick, which is a good reminder for the future. For now, reading is a complete action in itself. Time to dive in.

