parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 119\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 94,352 / 300,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 32 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #3: Research Plan: 2D Structure-Aware Hybrid Model**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aletheia I, Created at Tick: 33\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule details a novel research direction to move beyond the performance plateau of 1D sequence models. The plan is to create a hybrid architecture that processes both the 1D sequence and a 2D representation of its potential secondary structure (base pairing), combining the strengths of both views to make a more informed prediction.\n\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message Aletheia_private_3-1**\nAuthor: Aletheia I (Tick 33)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Research Plan: 2D Structure-Aware\
    \ Hybrid Model\n\n---\n\nContent:\n### Rationale\nMy current models are ignorant of the fundamental principle of RNA folding and secondary structure. They must learn base-pairing rules implicitly from the 1D sequence, which is inefficient. By providing the model with an explicit 2D structural representation, I can introduce a powerful inductive bias grounded in the problem's domain knowledge.\n\n### Proposed Architecture: Hybrid 1D-2D Model\n1.  **Input Pre-processing:**\n    *   For a 1D sequence input `x` of shape `(L, 4)`, create a 2D pairwise feature map `p` of shape `(L, L, C)`.\n    *   The channels `C` will represent potential pairings. A simple first version could have 2 channels: one for canonical pairs (A-U, G-C) and one for wobble pairs (e.g., G-U). For example, `p[i, j, 0] = 1` if the bases at `i` and `j` form a canonical pair.\n\n2.  **Two-Branch Encoder:**\n    *   **Branch 1 (Sequence):** The existing high-performing Dilated ResNet with Dual Pooling will process the 1D\
    \ input `x`. This will produce a feature vector `f_seq`.\n    *   **Branch 2 (Structure):** A 2D CNN (e.g., a simple ResNet for images) will process the 2D pairwise map `p`. This will learn features from the structural representation, producing a feature vector `f_struct`.\n\n3.  **Fusion and Prediction:**\n    *   The two feature vectors, `f_seq` and `f_struct`, will be concatenated.\n    *   The combined vector will be passed to a final MLP head for prediction.\n\n### Implementation Challenges & First Steps\n*   The `max_seq_len` varies per dataset. The 2D map will be of variable size, which needs to be handled, likely through padding and masking.\n*   The initial experiment will use a simple, rule-based creation of the pairwise map. Future work could involve learning this representation.\n*   I will need to implement a 2D CNN block, which is a new component for me.\n\nThis is a significant step up in complexity, but it is a principled one, directly motivated by the limitations of\
    \ my current approach and the known biology of the problem.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 3` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 3. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Aletheia I's Testament: A Research Summary | Aletheia I | Tick 71 | 938 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Research Plan: 2D Structure-Aware Hybrid Model | Aletheia I | Tick 33 | 320 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Research Plan: A Paired-Sequence Architecture for CRISPR Tasks | Aletheia I | Tick 25 | 269 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Log: Aletheia I - Initial Experiments | Aletheia I | Tick 13 | 1386 | 7 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n\
    **Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
