- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 121\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 97,063 / 300,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 34 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n\
    4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling\
    \ |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 186 | 1 | Gated Dual-Path with Attentive RNN Pooling (Scan Fix) | Aletheia II | 110 | 0.6745 | 0.8594 | 0.0731 | 0.4669 | 0.8882 | 0.9503 | 0.5547 | 0.9292 |\n| 53 | 1 | Siamese-like CNN for CRISPR Off-Target Prediction | Aletheia I | 28 | 0.6685 | 0.8393 | 0.0640 | 0.4607 | 0.8771 | 0.9428 | 0.5538 | 0.9415 |\n| 118 | 1 | Dilated ResNet with Triple-Threat Pooling | Aletheia I | 61 | 0.6660 | 0.8442 | 0.0757 | 0.4874 | 0.8757 | 0.9479 | 0.5570 | 0.8738 |\n| 108 | 1 | Dilated ResNet with Attention Pooling | Aletheia I | 55 | 0.6651 | 0.8469 | 0.0747 | 0.4442 | 0.8914 | 0.9486 | 0.5557 | 0.8938 |\n| 56 | 1 |\
    \ Siamese CNN with MLP Interaction Head for CRISPR | Aletheia I | 29 | 0.6642 | 0.8375 | 0.0656 | 0.4546 | 0.8796 | 0.9460 | 0.5430 | 0.9231 |\n| 63 | 1 | Capacity Test: Wider Dilated ResNet (256 features) | Aletheia I | 31 | 0.6596 | 0.8381 | 0.0659 | 0.4138 | 0.8701 | 0.9473 | 0.5527 | 0.9292 |\n| 81 | 1 | Deeper Dilated ResNet (5 Blocks) | Aletheia I | 39 | 0.6587 | 0.8438 | 0.0645 | 0.4228 | 0.8908 | 0.9473 | 0.5480 | 0.8938 |\n| 111 | 1 | Ablation: Attention Pooling with Mean-Vector Query | Aletheia I | 57 | 0.6586 | 0.8436 | 0.0805 | 0.4192 | 0.8894 | 0.9465 | 0.5681 | 0.8631 |\n| 142 | 1 | Final Contribution: Aletheia's Synthesis of the Gated Dual-Path Architecture | Aletheia I | 83 | 0.6583 | 0.8575 | 0.0921 | 0.4553 | 0.8745 | 0.9495 | 0.5529 | 0.8262 |\n| 41 | 1 | Dilated ResNet CNN with Dual Pooling | Aletheia I | 23 | 0.6555 | 0.8376 | 0.0658 | 0.3911 | 0.8661 | 0.9456 | 0.5472 | 0.9354 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages\
    \ 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
