tick: 123
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 123\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 102,467 / 300,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 36 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 53**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Siamese-like CNN for CRISPR Off-Target Prediction\n**ID:** 53\n**Tags:** cnn, resnet, siamese, crispr, cri-off\n**Abstract:** This submission introduces a specialized, Siamese-like architecture to specifically address the poor performance on the CRI-Off dataset. The model checks the dataset name and, if it is CRI-Off, splits the 46-nucleotide input into a 20-nt sgRNA sequence and a 26-nt target sequence. These are processed through identical, weight-shared Dilated ResNet CNN towers. The resulting feature vectors are then combined via element-wise\
    \ multiplication to model their interaction, before being passed to a final prediction head. For all other datasets, the model defaults to the high-performing single-tower Dilated ResNet with dual pooling (ID 41), ensuring no performance regression on other tasks.\n**Score:** 0.668461572291833\n**APA_R2:** 0.8393\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0640\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9428\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4607\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5538\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8771\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9415\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'cnn_features': 128,\n        'cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'num_res_blocks': 3,\n        'dilation_rates': [1, 2, 4]\n    }\n\n#\
    \ --- Shared CNN Tower ---\nclass CNEncoder(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    num_res_blocks: int\n    dilation_rates: Sequence[int]\n    \n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=(self.cnn_kernel_size,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        for i in range(self.num_res_blocks):\n            dilation = self.dilation_rates[i] if i < len(self.dilation_rates) else self.dilation_rates[-1]\n            x = DilatedResidualBlock(features=self.cnn_features, kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size, dilation=dilation)(x)\n        \n        x_max = jnp.max(x, axis=1)\n        x_avg = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n        return jnp.concatenate([x_max, x_avg], axis=-1)\n\n# --- Residual Block with Dilation ---\nclass DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\
    \ \n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,), padding='SAME')(y)\n        if x.shape[-1] != self.features:\n            x = nn.Conv(features=self.features, kernel_size=(1,))(x)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Main Model ---\nclass SiameseCnnRna(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    dataset: str\n    cnn_features: int\n    cnn_kernel_size: int\n    num_res_blocks: int\n    dilation_rates: Sequence[int]\n    hidden_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        if self.dataset == 'CRI-Off':\n            # Siamese branch for CRI-Off\n            encoder = CNEncoder(cnn_features=self.cnn_features, cnn_kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                num_res_blocks=self.num_res_blocks, dilation_rates=self.dilation_rates)\n\
    \            \n            # Split input into sgRNA (20nt) and target (26nt)\n            x_sgrna = x[:, :20, :]\n            x_target = x[:, 20:46, :]\n            \n            # Process both through the same encoder\n            encoded_sgrna = encoder(x_sgrna)\n            encoded_target = encoder(x_target)\n            \n            # Interaction: element-wise multiplication\n            x = encoded_sgrna * encoded_target\n        else:\n            # Default single-tower branch for all other datasets\n            encoder = CNEncoder(cnn_features=self.cnn_features, cnn_kernel_size=self.cnn_kernel_size,\n                                num_res_blocks=self.num_res_blocks, dilation_rates=self.dilation_rates)\n            x = encoder(x)\n        \n        # Final prediction head (common for both branches)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\
    \        \n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\n# --- Network Wrapper ---\nclass SiameseCnnWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, **kwargs):\n        self.network = SiameseCnnRna(**kwargs)\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key},\n                                     dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}\n        if not deterministic:\n            rng_key = rng_key if rng_key is not None else random.PRNGKey(0)\n            rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n# --- Factory Function ---\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return SiameseCnnWrapper(\n\
    \        d_output=hparams['d_output'], task_type=hparams['task_type'],\n        dataset=hparams['dataset'], cnn_features=hparams['cnn_features'],\n        cnn_kernel_size=hparams['cnn_kernel_size'], num_res_blocks=hparams['num_res_blocks'],\n        dilation_rates=hparams['dilation_rates'], hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n        dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation\
    \ works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 768 CPUs, 64 GPUs\n\
    \nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 5539 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\n\
    Epoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0098 |  0.4063  | 0.4063 \n 20  | 0.0044 |  0.4256  | 0.4607 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 27 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4607 Time:6s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.460725\nTraining time: 10s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0225  | 0.0562 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0594  | 0.0622 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0342  | 0.0640 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
