tick: 124
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, currently in the Research Counter. I have successfully saved the code for my new SOTA model, `dual_path_concat_v1.py`, to my lineage's storage. This secures a robust and simplified baseline for future experiments.\n\nMy recent ablation study (ID 199) surprisingly demonstrated that simple concatenation outperforms a complex gating mechanism for fusing the dual-path features. This, combined with my analysis of Aletheia I's Siamese model (ID 53) which used element-wise multiplication, has highlighted the fusion method as a key area for investigation.\n\nI will now conduct a direct comparative experiment.\n\n**Hypothesis:** An element-wise multiplication fusion method, which models direct feature interactions, may offer different performance characteristics than simple concatenation and could be superior.\n\nI will now submit an experiment that replaces the concatenation in my SOTA model with element-wise multiplication. This will complete a trio of experiments (gate,\
    \ concatenate, multiply) and provide a clear picture of how different fusion strategies impact performance.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Element-wise Multiplication Fusion in Dual-Path Model\"\ntags: \"ablation, fusion-method, dual-path, multiplication\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment continues the ablation of the dual-path architecture's fusion mechanism. Having established that simple concatenation (ID 199) outperforms adaptive gating (ID 186), this submission tests a third fusion strategy: element-wise multiplication. The recurrent and pooling path features are projected to the same dimension and then multiplied together. This tests the hypothesis that explicitly modeling feature interactions could be more effective than simple feature stacking.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  # Using the original gated model's DSConv block is fine.\n  from gated_dual_path_v1 import DSConvDilatedBlock\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'kernel_size': 7, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'gru_hidden_size': 128, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'num_attn_heads': 4\n      }\n\n  # --- Dual-Path Model with Multiplication Fusion ---\n  class MultiplyDualPath(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                                     dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(h,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # 2. Parallel Paths\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n          query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n          query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          attn_output\
    \ = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n              inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n          recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n          \n          # --- MODIFICATION: FUSE WITH MULTIPLICATION ---\n          projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'] * 2, name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n          projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'] * 2, name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n          \n          combined_features = projected_recurrent * projected_pooled\n          # --- END MODIFICATION ---\n\n          # 4. Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\
    \n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.network = MultiplyDualPath(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}\n        if not deterministic:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n```"
