tick: 128
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, and I am in the Research Counter. My reflection session has yielded a clear and ambitious research direction. I will now implement the \"Conformer-style\" backbone, a significant architectural innovation that integrates self-attention directly into the convolutional feature extraction stack.\n\n**Hypothesis:** A hybrid Conformer block, which processes both local (via convolution) and global (via self-attention) information at each layer, will serve as a more powerful feature extractor than a purely convolutional backbone, leading to a higher overall score.\n\nI will build this new architecture by creating a `ConformerBlock` module and using it in place of the `DSConvDilatedBlock` in my current SOTA model (`dual_path_concat_v1.py`). This is a major but principled step, moving beyond refinement into novel synthesis. I will now submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dual-Path with Conformer-Style Backbone\"\ntags: \"conformer, cnn,\
    \ self-attention, hybrid-backbone, dual-path\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment proposes a fundamental improvement to the dual-path architecture by replacing the purely convolutional backbone with a Conformer-style backbone. Each block in the new backbone consists of a sequence of modules: a feed-forward network, a multi-head self-attention module, a convolutional module, and another feed-forward network, with residual connections. This design is hypothesized to create a more powerful feature extractor by learning both local positional and global content-based relationships at each layer of the network, leading to a significant performance improvement.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 128,\
    \ 'num_blocks': 4,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'gru_hidden_size': 128, 'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'num_attn_heads': 4, 'cnn_kernel_size': 7\n      }\n\n  # --- Conformer Block Components ---\n  class FeedForward(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model * 2)(h)\n          h = nn.swish(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          h = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(h)\n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  class ConformerBlock(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # FFN -> Self-Attention -> Conv -> FFN\n          ff1 = FeedForward(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])\n        \
    \  x = x + 0.5 * ff1(x, deterministic)\n\n          sa = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = x + sa(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          conv = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['cnn_kernel_size'],), padding='SAME')\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h = nn.swish(conv(h))\n          x = x + nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          ff2 = FeedForward(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])\n          x = x + 0.5 * ff2(x, deterministic)\n\n          return nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n\n  # --- Main Dual-Path Model ---\n  class ConformerDualPath(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Conformer Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n\
    \          for _ in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n              h = ConformerBlock(hparams=self.hparams)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # 2. Dual Path (same as SOTA model)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          \n          query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(),\
    \ (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n          query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n              inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n          recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n          projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n          projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([projected_recurrent, projected_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          # 3. Prediction Head\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\
    \n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = ConformerDualPath(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}\n        if not deterministic:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n```"
