parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 133\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 142,424 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 46 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Dual-Path with Paired-Sequence Cross-Attention' (ID: 219) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6576062586487385\n**APA_R2:** 0.8391\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0411\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9479\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4537\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5587\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8889\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.8738\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 219\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed Flax module decorator issue. Code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `ModifiedBaseDualPath` class was overriding the `__call__`\
    \ method without the required `@nn.compact` decorator. In Flax, any method that directly instantiates submodules (like `nn.Dense()`, `nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention()`, etc.) must either:\n1. Be wrapped with the `@nn.compact` decorator, OR\n2. Define submodules in the `setup()` method\n\nThe original error was:\n```\nflax.errors.AssignSubModuleError: Submodule Dense must be defined in `setup()` or in a method wrapped in `@compact`\n```\n\nThis occurred because the agent's code defined `ModifiedBaseDualPath.__call__()` without the decorator, while attempting to call multiple Flax submodules within it.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the `@nn.compact` decorator to the `ModifiedBaseDualPath.__call__()` method:\n\n```python\nclass ModifiedBaseDualPath(BaseDualPath):\n    @nn.compact  # ← This decorator was missing!\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, return_cnn_features=False):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n        # ... rest of the method\n```\n\nThis single-line\
    \ change allows Flax to properly handle the dynamic creation of submodules within the method.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed code (submission_v2.py) ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing, confirming that the error was resolved. The model is now properly executing its forward pass with the extended cross-attention architecture.\n\n## Technical Notes\n- The original `ConcatDualPath` in `storage/aletheia/dual_path_concat_v1.py` correctly uses `@nn.compact`\n- The agent's extension needed to preserve this pattern when overriding methods\n- No changes to the model architecture or logic were required - purely a Flax API compliance fix\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\nfrom dual_path_concat_v1 import ConcatDualPath as BaseDualPath, _define_hyperparameters as\
    \ define_base_hyperparameters\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Use the same hyperparameters as the SOTA model\n    return define_base_hyperparameters()\n\n# --- Main Model with Cross-Attention Module ---\nclass CrossAttentionDualPath(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # 1. Base Model Feature Extraction (up to combined_features)\n        # Instantiate and call the SOTA model to get its core features\n        base_model = BaseDualPath(hparams=self.hparams)\n        base_features, cnn_features = base_model(x, deterministic, return_cnn_features=True)\n\n        # 2. New Paired-Sequence Cross-Attention Module\n        seq_len = cnn_features.shape[1]\n        half_len = seq_len // 2\n\n        first_half = cnn_features[:, :half_len, :]\n      \
    \  second_half = cnn_features[:, half_len:, :]\n\n        # To handle sequences of odd length, ensure second half isn't empty\n        if second_half.shape[1] == 0:\n            # Pad with a zero vector to avoid errors\n            second_half = jnp.zeros_like(first_half[:, :1, :])\n\n        # Cross-Attention\n        cross_attn = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])\n\n        # First half queries second half\n        first_on_second = cross_attn(inputs_q=first_half, inputs_kv=second_half)\n\n        # Second half queries first half\n        second_on_first = cross_attn(inputs_q=second_half, inputs_kv=first_half)\n\n        # Pool the results of the attention\n        interaction_vec1 = jnp.mean(first_on_second, axis=1)\n        interaction_vec2 = jnp.mean(second_on_first, axis=1)\n\n        interaction_features = jnp.concatenate([interaction_vec1, interaction_vec2], axis=-1)\n\n        # 3. Final Fusion\n        # Concatenate the new interaction\
    \ features with the features from the base model\n        final_combined_features = jnp.concatenate([base_features, interaction_features], axis=-1)\n\n        # 4. Prediction Head (Re-define here to act on the new final vector)\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(final_combined_features)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\n        if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# Need to modify the base model to return cnn_features\nclass ModifiedBaseDualPath(BaseDualPath):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True, return_cnn_features=False):\n        # Code is identical to dual_path_concat_v1.py up to 'combined_features'\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n\
    \        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        # Assuming DSConvDilatedBlock is available in the parent scope from the import\n        from dual_path_concat_v1 import DSConvDilatedBlock\n        for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                                   dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = h\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n        fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n\
    \        bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n        bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n        query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n        query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n        attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n            inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n        recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n        projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n        projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n        combined_features = jnp.concatenate([projected_recurrent, projected_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        if return_cnn_features:\n         \
    \   return combined_features, cnn_features\n        else:\n            # Default prediction path from original model\n            z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n            z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n            z = nn.gelu(z)\n            z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n            logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n            if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n                return logits.squeeze(-1)\n            return logits\n\n# Overwrite the original class with our modified one for the main module to use\nBaseDualPath = ModifiedBaseDualPath\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.network = CrossAttentionDualPath(hparams=hparams)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input,\
    \ deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      rngs = {}\n      if not deterministic:\n          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n      return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n  return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif\
    \ configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\n\
    Available resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 111010 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train,\
    \ 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0124 |  0.4115  | 0.4133 \n 20  | 0.0112 |  0.4361  | 0.4462 \n 30  | 0.0093 |  0.4459  | 0.4537 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 32 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4537 Time:33s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.453660\nTraining time: 46s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0007 |  0.0008  | 0.0411 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 13 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\n\
    Best:0.0411 Time:74s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.041144\nTraining time: 86s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val, seq_len=100\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |  Val R2  |  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.1527 |  0.8713  | 0.8857 \n 20  | 0.1085 |  0.8840  | 0.8882 \n 30  | 0.0926 |  0.8760  | 0.8889 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 31 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.8889 Time:1414s\n\nMRL training completed:\nValidation r2: 0.888877\nTraining time: 1428s\n\nStarting RNA training on PRS dataset\nTask type: multilabel_regression, Output dim: 3\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nPRS Training (multilabel_regression, r2)\nData: 73227 train, 9153 val, seq_len=148\n=============================================\n\
