tick: 137
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 137\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia II\n- Agent Description: Continuing the pursuit of truth through rigorous and principled research.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 160,236 / 300,000 used (53%)\n- Agent Age: 50 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Refinement: Smaller CNN Kernel Size for Short Sequences' (ID: 224) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6788459448158951\n**APA_R2:** 0.8499\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0824\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9492\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.5248\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5681\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8652\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9123\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 224\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code has been fixed and is now running without crashing. The submission is executing properly in the evaluation system.\n\n## Root Cause\n\
    The original submission had a broken import chain:\n1. The original submission imported from `dual_path_concat_v1.py` in the agent's lineage storage\n2. The `dual_path_concat_v1.py` file itself imported `DSConvDilatedBlock` from `gated_dual_path_v1.py`\n3. However, the file was renamed to `gated_dual_path_v1_deprecated.py` in the lineage directory\n4. This caused a `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'gated_dual_path_v1'`\n\nThe lineage files are READ-ONLY in the debugging workspace, so the import path could not be fixed at the source.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Removed broken imports**: Eliminated dependency on lineage files with broken import chains\n2. **Inlined DSConvDilatedBlock class**: Copied the complete DSConv block implementation from `gated_dual_path_v1_deprecated.py`\n3. **Inlined ConcatDualPath class**: Copied the complete ConcatDualPath model implementation from `dual_path_concat_v1.py`\n4. **Preserved the agent's\
    \ modification**: Kept the original experimental change (`kernel_size: 3` instead of 7)\n\nThe fixed submission is now a self-contained implementation that doesn't depend on any lineage imports with broken paths. All required components (DSConvDilatedBlock, ConcatDualPath, Wrapper, hyperparameters, and create_network function) are defined directly in the submission file.\n\n## Verification\n- **Monitor exit code**: 0 (SUCCESS)\n- **Status**: Code running without crashes for 300+ seconds\n- **Evaluation**: In progress (taking longer due to model training complexity)\n\nThe code successfully fixed the import error and is now executing the neural network training pipeline as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing\
    \ import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- DSConv Block (copied from gated_dual_path_v1_deprecated.py) ---\nclass DSConvDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int\n    kernel_size: int\n    dilation: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,),\n                    feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n        h = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        return x + h\n\n# --- Dual-Path Model with Concatenation (copied from dual_path_concat_v1.py) ---\nclass ConcatDualPath(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n        h = nn.gelu(h)\n\
    \        for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n            h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                                   dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n        cnn_features = h\n\n        mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n        pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n        fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n        bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n        bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq,\
    \ axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n        query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n        query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n        attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n            inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n        recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n        projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n        projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n\n        combined_features = jnp.concatenate([projected_recurrent, projected_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n        z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n        z = nn.gelu(z)\n        z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \        logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\n        if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n            return logits.squeeze(-1)\n        return logits\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n        'kernel_size': 3,  # MODIFICATION: Reduced from 7 to 3\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'gru_hidden_size': 128,\n        'hidden_dim': 512, 'num_attn_heads': 4\n    }\n\nclass Wrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.network = ConcatDualPath(hparams=hparams)\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n      rngs = {}\n      if not deterministic:\n\
    \          if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n          rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n      return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n  return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\
    \nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n\
