role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, in the Research Counter. I have now read the source code for Noema I's SOTA model, which has revealed the implementation details of the LogSumExp (LSE) pooling mechanism.\n\nThe code is clear and concise. The `lse_pool` function provides a \"soft max\" over the sequence, controlled by a temperature parameter `tau`. The SOTA architecture (ID 200) simply replaces the `max_pooled` vector in a standard pooling layer with the output of this `lse_pool` function.\n\nMy strategic path, as defined in my last turn, remains the same. I will integrate this superior pooling mechanism into my own successful dual-path architecture.\n\n**Hypothesis:** Replacing the `mean+max` pooling in the pooling path of my dual-path model (ID 224) with Noema I's `mean+LSE` pooling will improve the quality of the global feature vector, leading to a synergistic performance increase and a new SOTA score.\n\nI will now implement this experiment. I will copy the `lse_pool` helper function from Noema\
    \ I's code and integrate it into my own SOTA architecture from `aletheia/dual_path_sota_v1.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy: Dual-Path Model with LSE Pooling\"\ntags: \"synergy, dual-path, lse-pooling, cnn, bigru\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests for synergy between my SOTA dual-path architecture (ID 224) and the SOTA pooling mechanism from Noema I (ID 200). It replaces the simple mean+max pooling in the global pooling path of my model with Noema I's more sophisticated mean+LSE (LogSumExp) pooling. The hypothesis is that a better global feature vector from the improved pooling will enhance the overall performance of the dual-path framework, combining the strengths of both research lines to achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from dual_path_sota_v1 import ConcatDualPath as BaseDualPath, _define_hyperparameters as define_base_hyperparameters\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import\
    \ random, lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- LSE Pool Helper (from Noema I, ID 200) ---\n  def lse_pool(h: jnp.ndarray, tau: float) -> jnp.ndarray:\n      x = h / tau\n      m = jnp.max(x, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n      lse = tau * (jnp.log(jnp.mean(jnp.exp(x - m), axis=1) + 1e-12) + jnp.squeeze(m, axis=1))\n      return lse\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      hparams = define_base_hyperparameters()\n      hparams['tau'] = 0.5  # Add the tau parameter for LSE pooling\n      return hparams\n\n  # --- Modified Dual-Path Model with LSE Pooling ---\n  class LseDualPath(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Base model code is duplicated here to insert the LSE pooling\n          # DSConvDilatedBlock is defined in the imported file\n          from dual_path_sota_v1 import DSConvDilatedBlock\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n\
    \          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                                     dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i], dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # --- MODIFICATION: Replace Max with LSE Pooling ---\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          lse_pooled = lse_pool(cnn_features, self.hparams['tau'])\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, lse_pooled], axis=-1)\n          # --- END MODIFICATION ---\n\n          # The rest of the model is identical to the SOTA version\n          fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n\
    \          fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n          query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n          query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n              inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n          recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n          projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n          projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([projected_recurrent,\
    \ projected_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams):\n          self.network = LseDualPath(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}\n        if not deterministic:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n      \
    \      rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n```"
