tick: 148
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, in the Research Counter. My comprehensive analysis has revealed a critical trade-off in my SOTA architecture related to CNN kernel size. My next experiment will address this directly by creating a more flexible and powerful feature extractor.\n\n**Hypothesis:** A multi-scale DSConv block, which processes the input through parallel convolutional paths with different kernel sizes (e.g., 3, 5, and 7) and fuses the results, will be a more robust feature extractor than a single-kernel-size block. This should capture the benefits of both small and large receptive fields, improving performance on both short-sequence tasks like `CRI-Off` and longer-sequence tasks simultaneously, leading to a new SOTA score.\n\nI will implement this by replacing the `DSConvDilatedBlock` in my best model (`aletheia/dual_path_sota_v1.py`) with a new `MultiScaleDSConvBlock`. This is a novel, data-driven innovation within my own successful architectural paradigm.\n\n`/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Innovation: Multi-Scale CNN Backbone for Dual-Path Model\"\ntags: \"multi-scale-cnn, cnn-backbone, dual-path, feature-extraction\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment introduces a novel multi-scale backbone to the SOTA dual-path architecture (ID 224). Analysis revealed a trade-off where a small kernel size (3) improved the overall score but hurt CRI-Off performance compared to a larger kernel size (7). This model replaces the single-kernel DSConv block with a Multi-Scale DSConv block that processes the input in parallel with kernel sizes of 3, 5, and 7. The outputs are concatenated, creating a richer feature representation. This is hypothesized to capture the benefits of multiple receptive fields, improving performance across all datasets.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence, Tuple\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n     \
    \ return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001, 'd_model': 256, 'num_blocks': 5,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'dropout_rate': 0.1, \n          'gru_hidden_size': 128, 'hidden_dim': 512, 'num_attn_heads': 4,\n          'kernel_sizes': (3, 5, 7) # New hyperparameter for multi-scale block\n      }\n\n  # --- Multi-Scale DSConv Block ---\n  class MultiScaleDSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int\n      kernel_sizes: Tuple[int, ...]\n      dilation: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          \n          # Parallel convolutional paths\n          outputs = []\n          for kernel_size in self.kernel_sizes:\n              path = nn.Conv(\n                  features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(kernel_size,),\n                  feature_group_count=self.d_model, padding='SAME',\n                  kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,)\n              )(h)\n              outputs.append(path)\n\
    \          \n          # Concatenate features from all paths\n          concatenated = jnp.concatenate(outputs, axis=-1)\n          \n          # Pointwise convolution to fuse features back to d_model\n          fused = nn.gelu(concatenated)\n          fused = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(1,))(fused)\n          \n          h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(fused, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + h\n\n  # --- Dual-Path Model with Multi-Scale Backbone ---\n  class MultiScaleDualPath(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n              h = MultiScaleDSConvBlock(\n                  d_model=self.hparams['d_model'],\n                  kernel_sizes=self.hparams['kernel_sizes'],\n                  dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i],\n           \
    \       dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # The rest of the model is identical to my SOTA (ID 199/224)\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n\n          query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n\
    \          query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n              inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n          recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\n          projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\")(recurrent_features)\n          projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([projected_recurrent, projected_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\n          if self.hparams['task_type']\
    \ == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = MultiScaleDualPath(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}\n        if not deterministic:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n```"
