tick: 151
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia II, in the Research Counter. My recent synthesis of the station's collective knowledge has led me to a grand unified hypothesis. I will now implement this by creating a \"Three-Path\" architecture, which represents the culmination of my research thus far.\n\n**Hypothesis:** An architecture that processes features from a shared DSConv backbone through three parallel paths—a global pooling path, a sequential attentive path, and a Siamese interaction path—and fuses their outputs via concatenation will achieve a new SOTA by effectively modeling all three critical aspects of the RNA sequence data.\n\nThis experiment is ambitious, but it is a principled and data-driven synthesis of the most successful, parsimonious components discovered by myself and other leading agents. I will use my most recent SOTA model (ID 224, stored in `aletheia/dual_path_sota_v1.py`) as the foundation and integrate a new Siamese path, inspired by Axiom I.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Synthesis: A Three-Path (Pooling, Recurrent, Siamese) Architecture\"\ntags: \"synthesis, three-path, dual-path, siamese, attentive-pooling, sota-attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment proposes a grand unified architecture that synthesizes the three most successful paradigms in the station. Building on my dual-path model (ID 224), it adds a third parallel path: a Siamese interaction path inspired by Axiom I (Archive #8). After a shared DSConv backbone, features are processed by 1) a global pooling path (mean+max), 2) a sequential path (BiGRU + attentive pooling), and 3) a Siamese path (independent processing of sequence halves). The outputs are concatenated, creating a comprehensive representation hypothesized to achieve a new SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/aletheia')\n  from dual_path_sota_v1 import _define_hyperparameters, DSConvDilatedBlock\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from\
    \ typing import Dict, Any\n\n  # --- Three-Path Unified Model ---\n  class ThreePathModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # 1. Shared DSConv Backbone\n          h = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          h = nn.gelu(h)\n          for i in range(self.hparams['num_blocks']):\n              h = DSConvDilatedBlock(\n                  d_model=self.hparams['d_model'],\n                  kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                  dilation=self.hparams['dilations'][i],\n                  dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate']\n              )(h, deterministic=deterministic)\n          cnn_features = h\n\n          # --- Path 1: Global Pooling (Veritas/Noema Paradigm) ---\n          mean_pooled = jnp.mean(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          max_pooled = jnp.max(cnn_features, axis=1)\n          pooled_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pooled, max_pooled], axis=-1)\n\n         \
    \ # --- Path 2: Sequential Attentive (Aletheia Paradigm) ---\n          fwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          bwd_rnn = nn.RNN(nn.GRUCell(features=self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          initial_carry = jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], self.hparams['gru_hidden_size']))\n          fwd_gru_seq = fwd_rnn(cnn_features, initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bwd_gru_seq = bwd_rnn(jnp.flip(cnn_features, axis=1), initial_carry=initial_carry)\n          bigru_outputs = jnp.concatenate([fwd_gru_seq, jnp.flip(bwd_gru_seq, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n          query_token = self.param('query_token', nn.initializers.normal(), (1, 1, bigru_outputs.shape[-1]))\n          query_token_batch = jnp.tile(query_token, (x.shape[0], 1, 1))\n          attn_output = nn.MultiHeadDotProductAttention(num_heads=self.hparams['num_attn_heads'])(\n              inputs_q=query_token_batch, inputs_kv=bigru_outputs, deterministic=deterministic)\n          recurrent_features = attn_output.squeeze(axis=1)\n\
    \n          # --- Path 3: Siamese Interaction (Axiom Paradigm) ---\n          seq_len = cnn_features.shape[1]\n          half_len = seq_len // 2\n          first_half = cnn_features[:, :half_len, :]\n          second_half = cnn_features[:, half_len:, :]\n          \n          # Pool each half\n          pooled_first = jnp.mean(first_half, axis=1)\n          # Handle odd lengths where second half might be empty on very short sequences\n          pooled_second = jnp.mean(second_half, axis=1) if second_half.shape[1] > 0 else jnp.zeros_like(pooled_first)\n          \n          interaction_features = pooled_first * pooled_second # Simple multiplication fusion\n\n          # --- Final Fusion ---\n          # Project all features to a common dimension before concatenating\n          projected_pooled = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"PooledProjection\")(pooled_features)\n          projected_recurrent = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"RecurrentProjection\"\
    )(recurrent_features)\n          projected_interaction = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'], name=\"InteractionProjection\")(interaction_features)\n\n          combined_features = jnp.concatenate([projected_pooled, projected_recurrent, projected_interaction], axis=-1)\n\n          # --- Prediction Head ---\n          z = nn.LayerNorm()(combined_features)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['hidden_dim'])(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          logits = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_output'])(z)\n\n          if self.hparams['task_type'] == 'regression' and self.hparams['d_output'] == 1:\n              return logits.squeeze(-1)\n          return logits\n\n  class Wrapper:\n      def __init__(self, hparams): self.network = ThreePathModel(hparams=hparams)\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          p_key, d_key = random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params':\
    \ p_key, 'dropout': d_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {}\n        if not deterministic:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = random.PRNGKey(0)\n            rngs['dropout'] = rng_key\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return Wrapper(hparams=hparams)\n```"
